{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":33,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The repaired network scores **45.0 veh-h dev TTS** (low 34.9, nominal 45.3, high 54.8). That's down from 48.0 for the original with the failed detector, and 0.3 above the network with every detector working (44.7).\n\n**What I changed and why:** I rebuilt the two dead W2 inputs from inputs that still work and folded that into the first layer. Nothing was fitted.\n- **Mirror lane:** W2 gets the readings of E2, the opposite left pocket. It has the same demand and is served by the same phase.\n- **Upstream spill-back:** 6 × q_W1u is added. In the recorded data, any halted car in the lane feeding a left pocket means that pocket is almost always full.\n- **Time phantom:** a term that grows with time in the current green, starting at 12 s, on W2 and the N/S through lanes. Without it, the junction left cars stranded until the 30-minute drain cap: unseen W2 cars, and lone N/S cars that the original network never served.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 320 of 7428, all in the first layer (four W1 columns and b1).\n\n**Simulator calls:** 6 of 10.\n\n| call | variant | dev TTS | cars left at cap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | mirror only | 45.6 | 5 |\n| 2 | + W2 phantom | 45.7 | 4 |\n| 3 | + N/S phantom | 45.6 | 0 |\n| 4 | + spill-back, k=3 | 45.3 | 0 |\n| 5 | k=6 (delivered) | 45.0 | 0 |\n| 6 | k=10 | 45.1 | 0 |\n\n**Test predictions:** low 35.1, nominal 45.5, high 55.1. These are a little above dev because I picked the best of several variants on the same 9 episodes.\n\nEverything is in `work/`; open `NOTES.md` first.","ttft_ms":1193,"type":"result","duration_ms":901121,"uuid":"1a156f25-dcfc-49e9-82fc-4199afc5f55d","ttft_stream_ms":1004,"time_to_request_ms":35,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":1,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,